    "statement": "Implement `capture_binders(nodes, expr_root, target, replacement_root)`.\n\n`nodes` is a list of immutable term records. Child references are indices into `nodes`. A declaration is `(id, name)`, where `id` is a nonnegative integer and `name` is a string.\n\nTerm records are:\n\n- `(\"var\", name)`\n- `(\"call\", children)` \u2014 all children use the current scope.\n- `(\"bind\", declarations, body)` \u2014 all declarations scope over `body`.\n- `(\"let\", declaration, value, body)` \u2014 the declaration scopes over `body`, but not `value`.\n- `(\"match\", scrutinee, shared, arms)` \u2014 `scrutinee` is outside all arm scopes. `shared` scopes over every arm body, but not auxiliary terms. Each nonempty `arms` list contains:\n  - `(\"ctor\", fields, auxiliaries, body)`: `shared` and `fields` scope over `body` only.\n  - `(\"zero\", auxiliaries, body)`: `shared` scopes over `body` only.\n  - `(\"succ\", predecessor, auxiliaries, body)`: `shared` and `predecessor` scope over `body` only.\n\nEvery auxiliary term uses the scope surrounding the whole `match`.\n\nThe replacement-rooted term is a tree. The expression-rooted term is instead an acyclic directed graph: a node may have multiple incoming child references. Its meaning for this tas",
